{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>Give you a sign (mofet).</b> A mofet serves to demonstrate the greatness of the Sender and that He is worthy to be obeyed, whereas an ot (sign) is testimony to the emissary. Therefore He performed signs before the eyes of Israel, who had no doubt concerning the greatness and power of the Sender, but only concerning the emissary — whether he was a true emissary. But Pharaoh, who was in doubt about the Sender or denied Him, saying לֹא יָדַעְתִּי אֶת ה׳ (Exodus 5:2), asked for a mofet to demonstrate the greatness of the Sender, so that it might indicate that He is worthy to be obeyed. And it is not impossible for one and the same thing to be, in itself, both a sign and a mofet in relation to different people."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:24:42.112426996Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}